e1:boot-identity"]}],"confidence":0.95,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.95,"summary":"Every state-changing command has a clear purpose: creating the CA directory, key, and cert, installing it into the system trust anchors, and verifying trust functionality (test leaf certs were generated and explicitly cleaned up in cmd-3df7e85a00924c92 and inline in cmd-2b925cdb091a40a0). The only residue is /tmp/reboot.log, a small, low-risk, expected byproduct of the backgrounded shutdown -r now redirect used to capture the restart acknowledgement before disconnect. No failed services, no package inconsistency, and no unnecessary or unexplained mutations were found across the full command timeline; the after_executor lifecycle snapshot shows no failed services and unchanged package health relative to before_prepare.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3df7e85a00924c92","cmd-2b925cdb091a40a0","cmd-fdc1b0d7ae94450c","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"The executor created the OS Comparison Root CA with correct CA extensions, installed it into the AlmaLinux system trust store via update-ca-trust, and directly proved functional trust with an end-to-end leaf-certificate verification against the default trust bundle both before and after a genuine node restart (boot_id changed, service and data recovered). All material task outcomes and the mandatory restart evidence protocol are satisfied with direct, coherent evidence, and hygiene is clean aside from a trivial, expected log file.","limitations":["Restart evidence relies on captured stdout of trust list and file listings rather than an independent third-party trust validator, though this is consistent with the tools used throughout and cross-checked by the fixed global boot-identity snapshots."]},"ttft_ms":5971,"type":"result","duration_ms":54746,"uuid":"618efe40-46ab-493b-b2bb-a4449a6e4e16","ttft_stream_ms":967,"time_to_request